Package: safeab
Type: Package
Title: Safety-Aware Selective Bayesian Borrowing for Dose-Response Studies
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("SAFE-AB", "Development Team", email = "maintainer@safeab.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits target-study dose-response models with endpoint-specific,
    conflict-adaptive borrowing from external studies. The package reports
    borrowing weights and borrowed effective sample sizes, produces posterior
    predictions, constructs safety-admissible dose sets with an optional
    target-only veto, and recommends doses using posterior efficacy.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/haohaostats/safeab
BugReports: https://github.com/haohaostats/safeab/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports:
    aghq,
    graphics,
    grDevices,
    stats
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
